The error occurred because the [Task](cci:2://file:///d:/AFterClass%20new/taskly-fe/src/types/task.ts:0:0-9:2) type defined the `status` property as **required**, but when you were calling [editTaskService](cci:1://file:///d:/AFterClass%20new/taskly-fe/src/services/task.ts:33:0-40:2) in [Dashboard.tsx](cci:7://file:///d:/AFterClass%20new/taskly-fe/src/pages/Dashboard.tsx:0:0-0:0), you were passing an object that only included `id`, `title`, `desc`, and `label`.

I have fixed this by performing the following actions:

### 1. Updated [Task](cci:2://file:///d:/AFterClass%20new/taskly-fe/src/types/task.ts:0:0-9:2) Type Definition
I modified [src/types/task.ts](cci:7://file:///d:/AFterClass%20new/taskly-fe/src/types/task.ts:0:0-0:0) to make the `status` property optional. Since neither the creation nor the editing services currently require or send a `status` to the backend, it shouldn't be a required field in the frontend model if it's not always available.

```typescript
// src/types/task.ts
export type Task = {
  id?: string;
  userId?: string;
  title: string;
  desc: string;
  label: string;
  status?: string; // Changed from required to optional
  createdAt?: Date;
  updatedAt?: Date;
};
```

### 2. Fixed `onClick` Bug in [Dashboard.tsx](cci:7://file:///d:/AFterClass%20new/taskly-fe/src/pages/Dashboard.tsx:0:0-0:0)
I noticed that the "Save Changes" button in your dialog was calling the functions immediately during render (`onClick={isEditing ? editTask() : createTask()}`) instead of passing them as references. This would cause the functions to fire every time the component rendered. I updated it to:
```tsx
<Button onClick={isEditing ? editTask : createTask}>
```

### 3. Improved Dialog Feedback
I also updated the `Input` and `Textarea` components in the dialog to be **controlled components** by adding the `value` prop. This ensures that when you click "Edit", the existing task data (title and description) correctly appears in the input fields.

