The build error was caused by the file `src/lib/utils.ts` being encoded in **UTF-16LE** instead of the standard **UTF-8**. Turbopack (and most web bundlers) expects source files to be UTF-8 and fails when encountering the null bytes or Byte Order Marks (BOM) present in UTF-16 encoding.

I have:
1.  **Read and verified** the encoding issue (confirmed by the system reporting an "unsupported mime type `text/plain; charset=utf-16le`").
2.  **Overwritten `src/lib/utils.ts`** with the correct `cn` utility function in **UTF-8** encoding.
3.  **Verified other key files** (`badge.tsx`, `ReportsFeed.tsx`, `api.ts`) to ensure they aren't affected by similar encoding problems.

The Next.js dev server should now be able to parse the source code and complete the build.

